---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const outcomes=[
{num:'01',title:'GEAR',subtitle:'Protection That Saves Lives',image:'/images/impact/gear-moto-foundation-impact-gear-protection-saves-lives.jpg',alt:'Illustrative GEAR protective equipment campaign showing motorcycle safety gear',desc:'A helmet or armored jacket can be the difference between a ride and a life-changing injury. Our aim is to help lower the cost barriers to protective equipment for riders who need it.',measure:'Riders equipped, qualifying protective equipment distributed, and partner-supported access.',link:'/programs/#gear'},
{num:'02',title:'EDUCATION',subtitle:'Skills. Safety. Confidence.',image:'/images/impact/gear-moto-foundation-our-impact-young-rider-safety-education.jpg',alt:'Illustrative young motorcycle rider learning safe riding skills with an instructor at a controlled training course',desc:'More confidence comes from better preparation. We intend to make approved rider training, skills development, and endorsement-related education more accessible.',measure:'Training awards, completed courses, and voluntarily reported endorsements.',link:'/programs/#education'},
{num:'03',title:'ASSISTANCE',subtitle:'Resources. Guidance. Connection.',image:'/images/impact/gear-moto-foundation-our-impact-rider-assistance-resources.jpg',alt:'Illustrative young rider receiving help with assistance paperwork at a motorcycle community event',desc:'A rider should not have to navigate every challenge alone. GEAR plans to connect riders and families with practical information, trusted resources, and relevant service providers.',measure:'Resource connections, referrals by category, and households assisted with navigation.',link:'/programs/#assistance'},
{num:'04',title:'RECOVERY',subtitle:'Relief. Recovery. Rebuilding.',image:'/images/impact/gear-moto-foundation-our-impact-injured-rider-recovery-support.jpg',alt:'Illustrative injured young motorcycle rider supported by friends during recovery after an accident',desc:'A serious crash can affect far more than the motorcycle. Our proposed Recovery program aims to address qualifying accident-related expenses, rehabilitation and hardship needs, and the long path toward rebuilding stability.',measure:'Approved medical and hardship awards, verified expenses relieved, and people supported during recovery.',link:'/programs/#recovery'}
];
---
<Base title="Our Impact" description="The impact GEAR Moto Foundation is working toward: protective gear, rider education, practical assistance, recovery support and accountable reporting.">
<section class="impact-lead"><div class="wrap impact-lead-grid"><div class="impact-lead-copy"><span class="impact-kicker">OUR IMPACT / OUR COMMITMENT</span><h1>THE MOST IMPORTANT PART OF THE RIDE <em>IS THE RIDER.</em></h1><p>We believe the strength of a motorcycle community is measured by how it protects, prepares and stands beside its people.</p><div class="impact-lead-actions"><a href="#impact-pillars" class="btn btn-red">The Difference We Want to Make ↗</a><a href="#impact-accountability" class="impact-text-link">How we'll report results ↓</a></div></div><figure class="impact-image"><img src="/images/impact/gear-moto-foundation-our-impact-young-sportbike-riders-community.jpg" alt="Illustrative diverse community of young sportbike riders in protective motorcycle gear gathered at sunset" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Illustrative campaign image representing our mission.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section class="impact-belief"><div class="wrap impact-belief-inner"><span class="impact-kicker">ALL BIKES. ALL RIDERS.</span><h2>BECAUSE BEHIND EVERY HELMET<br/>IS A PERSON WHO MATTERS.</h2><p>Every rider has a life beyond the road: friends, family, plans and a future. Our purpose is to bring practical help and community support closer to the moments that matter.</p></div></section>
<section class="impact-pillars-section" id="impact-pillars"><div class="wrap"><div class="impact-section-heading"><div><span class="impact-kicker">FOUR WAYS TO MAKE A DIFFERENCE</span><h2>THE IMPACT WE'RE<br/><em>BUILDING TOWARD.</em></h2></div><p>These are proposed areas of impact, not claims of assistance already delivered. Explore each pillar and the outcomes we intend to track.</p></div><nav class="impact-jump-nav" aria-label="Jump to an impact pillar"><a href="#impact-gear">Gear ↓</a><a href="#impact-education">Education ↓</a><a href="#impact-assistance">Assistance ↓</a><a href="#impact-recovery">Recovery ↓</a></nav>{outcomes.map((p,i)=><article class={'impact-story impact-story-'+i} id={'impact-'+p.title.toLowerCase()}><div class="impact-story-content"><span class="impact-story-index">{p.num} / 04 · {p.title}</span><h3>{p.subtitle}</h3><p>{p.desc}</p><details class="impact-outcome"><summary>What we'll measure <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{p.measure}</p></details><a href={p.link} class="impact-story-link">Explore {p.title.charAt(0)+p.title.slice(1).toLowerCase()} ↗</a></div><figure class="impact-image impact-story-image"><img src={p.image} alt={p.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>Illustrative concept imagery — not a documented GEAR program result.</figcaption></figure></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="impact-accountability" id="impact-accountability"><div class="wrap"><div class="impact-section-heading"><div><span class="impact-kicker">MEANINGFUL IMPACT REQUIRES ACCOUNTABILITY</span><h2>NOT JUST GOOD INTENTIONS.<br/><em>REAL TRANSPARENCY.</em></h2></div><p>Community trust comes from reporting what actually happened—not simply what we hoped would happen.</p></div><div class="impact-principles"><article><span>01</span><h3>Verified Results</h3><p>We will distinguish completed activities and documented outcomes from goals, proposals and projections.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Responsible Stewardship</h3><p>We intend to report charitable spending, event activity, contributions, and how resources support each program.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Fair Decisions</h3><p>Objective eligibility policies, conflict safeguards and appropriate independent board oversight will guide program decisions.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Privacy & Dignity</h3><p>People seeking support deserve confidentiality. No recipient will be required to share a personal story publicly.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="impact-reporting"><div class="wrap impact-report-grid"><div><span class="impact-kicker">OUR CURRENT STATUS</span><h2>THE STORY IS<br/><em>JUST BEGINNING.</em></h2><p>We are developing the foundation, its operational policies, partnerships and future programs. We have not published operating grant results and are not accepting public grant applications.</p></div><div class="impact-report-box"><h3>What you'll eventually find here</h3><ul><li>Verified program outcomes across all four pillars</li><li>Financial stewardship and relevant public filings</li><li>Events, partnerships and volunteer activity</li><li>Approved program policies and progress reports</li></ul><p><strong>Formation and filings:</strong> Draft bylaws, plans and five-year forecasts are not evidence of incorporation, IRS recognition, adopted policies or actual financial performance. Official documents will be published when finalized and approved.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="impact-close"><div class="wrap"><span class="impact-kicker">RIDERS HELPING RIDERS</span><h2>LET'S BUILD SOMETHING<br/><em>THAT LASTS BEYOND THE RIDE.</em></h2><p>The next chapter of GEAR will be shaped by riders, supporters and community partners who believe every rider matters.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-red" href="/volunteer/">Get Involved ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline-dark" href="/partners/">Explore Partnerships ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline-dark" href="/contact/">Ask a Transparency Question ↗</a></div></div></section>
</Base>